Z||000000||Philphine||11-26-2001||08:01 PM||||<BR>got one in my '87 and didn't want to fool with it in my '86, but i'm wanting to include it in my plans more and more. i don't feel like pulling out the dash to do it so i'm wondering if anyone else has one and how they worked it. got a couple ideas if i can find the right speaker but any other ideas appreciated.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||11-26-2001||08:32 PM||||Top of the sub box?  Custom enclosure in front of the 3<sup>rd</sup> brake light (incorporate the brake light)?  If you're using a DIN size head unit, why not make a custom mounting for it raising it to the top of the opening, then fabbing an angled mount just under it (from the bottom of the head unit to the front of the shifter area)?  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||11-26-2001||08:57 PM||||Center channel needs to be in the front for correct staging. Idea's I have seen in the past are:<BR>In the center vent<BR>The space between the shift console and the radio pod.<BR>Center of the upper dash.<BR>On top of the radio pod (one without the extra gauges)<BR>Between the extra gauges and the dash facing up.<BR>Inside the rear view mirror. (they bought an aftermarket mirror and stuffed in a pair of 1" soft dome tweeters and wired them in series so they were each the same out.)<P>Remember that center channel is only the Left minus Right of the mid range freq's (about 2khz to 4khz). You do not need a full range speaker.  <P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||11-27-2001||05:37 AM||||i'm thinking right now a 4" if i can find one of two i'm thinking of. i tried once putting two 3" speakers in a big rear view mirror, but it fell off the window constantly till i reworked it to attatch to the roof (my blazer). <P>thats what i'm thinking again but i'm going to keep an eye out for an illusion audio 4" or an infinity 4" that was made a few years back similar to the illusions. hopefully a single lighter design speaker as part of a normal mirror might stay.||||reg||1
